Day 7 — GCP Kubernetes (GKE) Production + Security + Scaling

Scenario-Based DevOps Interview Questions

1️⃣ Your GKE cluster is running multiple microservices. One service is consuming more CPU causing noisy-neighbour issues. How will you control and stabilize resources?

2️⃣ A workload requires zero downtime upgrades even during peak traffic. How will you design deployment strategy (Rolling, Blue-Green, Canary)?

3️⃣ You need auto-healing + auto-scaling + PDB (Pod Disruption Budget) protection for a production service. How will you configure all three together?

4️⃣ Your cluster nodes are over-provisioned leading to high cost. How will you optimize with Node Autoscaling + Cluster Autoscaler + Pod requests/limits tuning?

5️⃣ Secrets are currently stored as plain K8s secrets. How will you secure them using KMS + Workload Identity + Secret Manager integration?

6️⃣ A pod is stuck in Pending state. How will you troubleshoot (nodes, taints/tolerations, quotas, CNI, storage, limits)?

7️⃣ Developers need namespace-level access only with RBAC control. How will you design roles, rolebindings, service accounts, and policies?

8️⃣ A service must store logs for 30 days and expose metrics to Prometheus with dashboards in Grafana. How will you integrate logging + monitoring stack?

9️⃣ You have heavy periodic jobs running on GKE. How will you optimize using Spot nodes with graceful eviction strategy?

🔟 A service needs high and bursty throughput. Will you choose Horizontal Pod Autoscaler, Vertical Pod Autoscaler or both? Justify your design.

1️⃣1️⃣ Application rollout failed and new pods are crashing. How will you quickly rollback and debug?

1️⃣2️⃣ You need end-to-end mTLS inside cluster between microservices. How will you implement this using Istio/Anthos Service Mesh?

1️⃣3️⃣ Traffic should be routed based on specific header values. Which Ingress + Gateway API configuration will you use?

1️⃣4️⃣ You need cross-cluster deployment spanning multi-region for DR. How will you architect this using Fleet/Anthos/GCLB?

1️⃣5️⃣ Pods need access to Cloud SQL without exposing credentials. How will you integrate Cloud SQL Auth Proxy + Workload Identity?
